From 87ff87f91504cecc2625a37618d080da3fc5bb01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rehan Ganapathy <rehang1710@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:44:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Warn at startup and in the UI when the datastore is not on a
 persistent volume

The Docker image has no VOLUME for /datastore, so a container started without
-v (or a compose/PaaS template missing the volumes: entry) writes every watch
and setting into its writable layer. It survives 'docker restart' but is lost
on the next re-create (image update, redeploy), which users see as watches and
settings randomly disappearing.

Detect this on Linux by checking /proc/self/mountinfo: if the datastore lives
on the container's overlay root, log a CRITICAL message at startup and show a
banner in the UI. Opt out with DISABLE_DATASTORE_STORAGE_CHECK=true.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qYNnEyN6pCfhgAjjvArHS
